Nyxoah markets their open-loop bilateral hypoglossal nerve stimulation device, described above in certain countries, and LivaNova also markets an open-loop neurostimulation device outside the U.S.

Additionally, a drug candidate produced by Apnimed is undergoing a Phase 3 clinical trial to assess the viability of its pharmaceutical to treat OSA. In December 2024, the GLP-1 drug Zepbound (tirzepatide), was FDA approved for treatment of OSA in patients with obesity and moderate to severe OSA. We believe other emerging businesses are in the early stages of developing alternative OSA treatment therapies or early-stage pharmaceutical approaches.

